module Core

### Represents the coarse-grained state exposed by a lock policy.
### These values describe the externally visible access mode of a controller,
### not the full internal implementation strategy.
choice LockState
  ### No active readers or writers; the lock is available for acquisition.
  IDLE
  ### One or more readers hold shared access; writers are excluded.
  READING
  ### A single writer holds exclusive access; all other accessors are excluded.
  WRITING

### Represents a policy object that can report lock-controller state.
### Concrete policies define how concurrent readers and writers are coordinated,
### while this protocol provides a shared observation surface for diagnostics and
### runtime checks.
protocol LockPolicy
  ### Returns the current lock state.
  ### This is intended for coordination logic and diagnostics rather than for
  ### enforcing synchronization by itself.
  ### :returns: The resulting `LockState` value.
  routine Me.state() -> LockState
